version: 2.0.0
description: |
  Utility modules for the MCP server — loaders, caches, and data access.
components:
  gnomon-staged:
    description: >-
      #gnomon-staged (TD-2026-10-27-833): utils/gnomon-staged.ts, the mode the Gnomon kernel sets
      (PARADIGM_GNOMON_STAGED=1) when it runs the staged single-file bundle for a LOCAL model session. In that mode
      the server skips Conductor auto-registration (ps/osascript, a global-dir write) and refuses
      paradigm_plugin_check (it shells out and reaches the network). The global dir follows HOME (the kernel points it
      at an empty per-session kernel-owned dir); git hardening comes from the kernel's GIT_CONFIG_* env. Paradigm loads
      no .paradigm/ file as code in any mode (audited: habits, protocols, config, loops are data; loop checks run only
      in the Gnomon kernel after a human trusts the exact content hash).
      Aegis review fixes: H2 breadcrumbBase puts breadcrumbs, the session work
      log, postflight liveness and verdicts under HOME; no background static
      index rebuild per call (index-loader) and no university pack cache
      (university-core) in the staged mode. M1 staged-guard.ts wraps Node's fs
      write/read API once at start: writes only to <root>/.paradigm/**, .purpose
      files, the root portal.yaml and HOME (never .git, never via a symlink),
      reads only in the root, HOME and the bundle dir. M2 STAGED_REFUSED_FAMILIES
      (persona, symphony, platform, conductor, brain, sentinel) are unlisted,
      unannotated and refused. aspect suggest_scan refuses (unbundlable import).
    path: src/utils/gnomon-staged.ts
    type: module
    tags: [mcp, gnomon, td-2026-10-27-833]
    tests:
      - src/tools/family-op-annotations.test.ts
      - src/tools/staged-ops.test.ts
      - src/utils/staged-guard.test.ts
  plugin-update-checker:
    description: >-
      #plugin-update-checker: detects stale Claude Code plugins (marketplace clones vs remote, cached
      install vs marketplace content hash). Output is inert data: PluginUpdateNotice
      {kind:'plugin-update', plugin, marketplace, repo, from, to, reason, command}, plus a
      descriptive, host-aware summary that never addresses the agent. detectPluginHost reads
      GNOMON_HSID (set by Gnomon's #session-runner on every session): a Gnomon session's summary
      names only the terminal command `claude plugin marketplace update <mkt> && claude plugin
      update <plugin>@<mkt>`; interactive Claude Code may also name /plugin. Reported only by
      paradigm_status check:'plugins' (legacy paradigm_plugin_check); never prepended to the
      first tool result of a session, and no background refresh runs on the first tool call.
    type: service
    anchors:
      - plugin-update-checker.ts
      - plugin-update-checker.test.ts
    tags: [plugins, host-aware, gnomon]
  context-freshness:
    description: >-
      #context-freshness (7.15.0, TD-2026-10-13-661 Phase 1): the MCP server's ProjectContext is
      backed by premise-core #live-index. index-loader.ts loadProjectContext uses getLiveIndex;
      ensureFreshContext (called at every getContext() choke point: tools/index.ts CallTool,
      resources/index.ts, resources/symbols.ts) swaps index/aggregation/gateConfig atomically
      in place when files changed on disk, shares one in-flight refresh per context and
      debounces checks (FRESHNESS_DEBOUNCE_MS = 500). Hand edits and git checkouts become visible
      without paradigm_reindex. tool-cache.ts bindIndex clears the result cache when the index
      changes, with a generation counter so late computes are not cached. Removed the dead
      ensureFreshIndex/isContextStale TTL path. integrity-checker.ts counts only declared symbols
      as defined and reports undeclared references (refType 'undeclared', warning, danglingCount
      in the reindex summary).
    type: loader
    anchors:
      - index-loader.ts
      - tool-cache.ts
      - integrity-checker.ts
    tags: [live-index, freshness, integrity]
  symphony-loader:
    description: 'The Score: file-based agent messaging — agent identity, JSONL parts, threads, file pipeline, trust config. ensureMailDirs renamed to ensureScoreDirs (deprecated alias retained). Ring 1 content filtering seam: isRing1Content, recordRing1Interception (audit trail), readOutboxRaw (unfiltered, relay-internal), readOutbox (filtered). SymphonyMessage.contentType field added.'
    type: loader
    anchors:
      - symphony-loader.ts:1-1205
    tags:
      - feature
      - symphony
  university-loader:
    description: 'Per-project university loader — CRUD for notes/policies/quizzes/paths/diplomas, index rebuild, validation, symbol linking for ripple. v6.0 sub-phase 1: accepts optional packRoot on all CRUD fns, walks discipline sub-packs via discoverDisciplineSubPacks, preserves v5 behavior via loadOrFabricatePackManifest (implicit pack when pack.yaml absent), stamps pack_id on writes. Pack-selector fix: resolveContentBase probes content/ + src/content/ (shared with countPackEntries); scanPackEntries is the single frontmatter→entry mapper used by both rebuildUniversityIndex (project, writes index) and loadPackIndex (selected pack, in-memory scan, no write); searchContent/getOnboardingSequence/validateUniversityContent take optional trailing packRoot — when present they read the selected pack, when omitted they keep the byte-identical project path. Deep-validate symbol/staleness/coverage checks stay rootDir-relative (project owns symbol authority).'
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - university
      - v6.0
  platform-bridge:
    description: HTTP bridge for MCP → Platform server communication. Resolves port from config.yaml, resolves agent identity, sends POST to /api/platform/agent-command.
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - platform
      - agent-ui
  symphony-peers:
    description: Peer trust records for Symphony cross-machine networking — peers.json CRUD, pairing code generation/verification, HMAC authentication.
    type: loader
    anchors:
      - symphony-peers.ts:1-229
    tags:
      - feature
      - symphony
      - networking
  symphony-relay:
    description: WebSocket relay engine for cross-machine Symphony networking — hub/spoke modes, outbox watcher, message routing, dedup, keepalive, auto-reconnect. Unsafe inline Ring 1 filter sites removed; delegates to symphony-loader for content filtering.
    type: integration
    anchors:
      - symphony-relay.ts:1-1000
    tags:
      - feature
      - symphony
      - networking
  agent-loader:
    description: "CRUD for .agent identity files — load/save profiles, expertise queries, auto-update from lore, merge with agents.yaml, sync from lore history, permission checking (path/tool), integrity hash computation/verification, integrity status at load time, prompt sanitization, permission constraint extraction, permission enforcement facade. v7.9.1 normalizeAgentProfile runs after every profile yaml.load — legacy transferable[].pattern becomes id (explicit id wins; pattern removed; migrated to id on next save), no other defaults injected (learnedIn/appliedIn stay optional; enrichment omits learned-in when absent); never touches id/role/permissions so integrityHash is unaffected. Skills Phase 1 (v7.10.0): buildProfileEnrichment takes a 6th optional skills?: SkillSummary[] (stays pure; callers resolve via #skill-loader resolveAgentSkills) and renders a '## Your Skills' section after Transferable Patterns — certified+ok for every agent, non-certified only to the steward (labelled), stale/invalid omitted; AgentProfile.skills is excluded from integrityHash"
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - agent-identity
      - permissions
      - security
  agent-registry:
    description: 'v7.9.1 (TD-2026-09-26-846) resolveDispatchableAgents(rootDir, opts?) — roster.yaml + loaded .agent profiles are authoritative for dispatch; .paradigm/agents.yaml is an optional overlay (role/focus/triggers/handoff_to/defaultModel/context/protocol override profile-derived values) and emits a one-time deprecation warning. Candidates = roster ids, else union(profile ids, agents.yaml ids). Benched profiles and roster members with neither profile nor agents.yaml entry are REPORTED as undispatchable, never dropped. Profile-derived definition: role = agents.yaml › ROLE_PROMPTS › profile.role; focus.reads = attention.paths; triggers = attention.concepts (keyword) + attention.symbols (symbol), tagged derived: true; handoff_to = partners › collaboration.with. Returns the parsed agents.yaml (manifest) for reuse and the orchestration block (default_mode, budget). Never deletes agents.yaml.'
    type: loader
    anchors:
      - agent-registry.ts
    tags:
      - feature
      - agent-identity
      - orchestration
  role-prompts:
    description: ROLE_PROMPTS — battle-tested role prompts for the core agents, extracted from tools/orchestration.ts so #agent-registry can use them without a circular import
    type: constant
    anchors:
      - role-prompts.ts
    tags:
      - orchestration
  notebook-loader:
    description: 'CRUD for agent notebook entries — load/save, search, promote from lore, increment applied count. The Classroom (TD-2026-06-19-007): reviseDown is the fail-side mutation (bumps appliedAndBrokeCount, lowers confidence, captures the "X except Y" refinement exception mechanically — prose authored at gated /paradigm:class refine, dedup by sourceFailureId); listAllAgentNotebookEntries + decayUnusedEntry are the decay-pass enumerate/mutate seams.'
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - notebooks
      - agent-identity
      - classroom
    components:
      - '#soft-provenance'
  classroom-decay:
    description: 'The Classroom decay pass (TD-2026-06-19-007, Phase 2) — load-bearing for the metric, not cleanup. Flips pending certs aged past the SURVIVAL_WINDOW (14d) with no attributed break to outcome:survived (makes repeat-failure-rate''s resolved denominator real instead of a structural 1.0); gently decays confidence of entries idle past IDLE_WINDOW (30d) with low appliedCount (silence is signal; never deletes). runDecayPass is best-effort/idempotent, wired into ambient postflight right after runFieldFailureReducer.'
    type: service
    anchors:
      - decay.ts:1-200
    tags:
      - feature
      - classroom
      - learning-loop
  classroom-fail-side:
    description: 'The Classroom fail-side event writers + reducer (TD-2026-06-19-007). field-failures.ts: append-only field-failures.jsonl + classroom-certifications.jsonl; overturnCertification (pending→overturned) and surviveCertification (pending→survived, decay-pass writer) — both idempotent, overturn wins. field-failure-reducer.ts: joins reviewer verdicts to notebook-refs by orchestrationId, revises down, back-binds certs, seeds field-failure scenarios.'
    type: service
    anchors:
      - field-failures.ts:1-290
      - field-failure-reducer.ts:1-213
    tags:
      - feature
      - classroom
      - learning-loop
  loop-files:
    description: >-
      #loop-files (Gnomon loops LP1, docs/specs/gnomon-loops.md §2/§5): repo loop definition files.
      .paradigm/loops/<id>.yaml is parsed with js-yaml (CORE schema), validated and compiled by
      #loop-schema (@a-company/gnomon/loops) with the other repo loops (call cycles, depth, unknown
      callees) and the flow index (.paradigm/flow-index.json; a flow resolves to its defining
      .purpose dir plus each step symbol's .purpose dir from scan-index.json), and the id must match
      the file name. On success <id>.loop.json (canonical key order, indented) is written beside the
      YAML; on failure a stale one is removed so the kernel never reads a definition the YAML no
      longer says. writeLoop (create/update), validateLoopFile/validateAllLoops, listLoops (fresh,
      stale, missing), getLoop and defaultTemplateFlow (the templates are #loop-templates). A flow
      index written on Windows (backslash paths) is normalized before it resolves, so a flow never
      widens to ** on another platform; another machine's drive path resolves to nothing. Shared
      by #loop-cli and #loop-mcp. Hardened (Aegis LP1): symlinks refused for .paradigm, the loops
      dir and every loop file; the dir's realpath must be the repo's .paradigm/loops; validate takes
      only files directly in it; writes go temp + rename and never through a symlink; stale JSON is
      removed even with write:false; orphan .loop.json (YAML gone) listed and removed by validate
      all; readShebangAt records argv0Interpreter.
    type: loader
    anchors:
      - loop-files.ts
    tags: [feature, gnomon, loops]
  loop-templates:
    description: >-
      #loop-templates (Gnomon loops LP9, build plan step 14; docs/specs/gnomon-loops.md §2 Examples
      A-D): the loop:v2 starting points behind `paradigm loop new <id> --template <name>` and
      paradigm_loop create {template}. flow-health (Example A: read-only flow, .purpose and drift
      checks, a local summary toast), green (Example B on a local model: tsc -p <dir>/tsconfig.json,
      a local act step, every change a propose card), watch (Example C on a file trigger), tidy
      (Example D in its 8.0 form: reindex and .purpose validation on a private copy plus a local
      digest; reports only, because write checks are not in 8.0), and a minimal starter. All valid
      under the 8.0 validator and runnable by the 8.0 runner (local models only, no write checks);
      the wording fits approve-to-land (TD-2026-10-22-369): no template promises to land on its own.
      green names the tsconfig FILE, because an argv path is protected from act edits and a
      wildcard-free protected path covers everything beneath it. Parameters (flow, dir) are checked
      against closed patterns before they reach YAML (TemplateParamError). Each template's compiled
      hashes are pinned in its test.
    type: utility
    anchors:
      - loop-templates.ts
    tests:
      - loop-templates.test.ts
    tags: [feature, gnomon, loops]
  tool-family:
    description: '7.13 defineFamily({name, description, ops}) — builds one listed tool whose schema is an op enum + compacted union of the legacy tools'' properties (property descriptions omitted for budget; nested item/object shapes kept as names + required; op signatures in the description: full for signatures:''full'' families, required-only otherwise; HANDLER_DEFAULTED exempts handler-defaulted params from per-op validation), with runtime per-op required validation that echoes the op''s params. Also canonicalizeToolRef (legacy / family.op / family({op}) / bare family → canonical legacy names) used by habits evaluation, and compactDefinition for anchors. Per-op annotations (S-P, TD-2026-10-27-833): each ToolFamily carries opAnnotations = { <op>: the readOnly/destructive/idempotent/openWorld hints that op''s legacy definition DECLARES } (declaredOpHints; ops declaring none are omitted; consumers read a missing op as mutate). It is NOT in the listed definition (no tools/list _meta); it is served by the paradigm://tool-annotations resource (OP_ANNOTATIONS_RESOURCE_URI, schema OP_ANNOTATIONS_SCHEMA io.gnomon/op-annotations:v1). Top-level annotations hold for every op (familyAnnotations): readOnlyHint only if all ops are read-only; destructiveHint false only if every op is read-only or declares destructiveHint:false (an undeclared op counts as destructive, the MCP default); idempotentHint only if all ops declare it; openWorldHint true if any op does.'
    type: utility
    tags:
      - feature
      - mcp
      - tool-surface
  tool-registry:
    description: 'Tiered tool registration system — core/feature/advanced tiers with auto-detection. getAllTools() lists every module regardless of tier (backs listToolDefinitions for skill pin checks). v7.11: university detection is pack-based (detectUniversityPacks — a discovered pack with entries or skillDirs, or an implicit v5 project pack with content; requires .paradigm; fail-closed false) — an empty scaffold no longer activates the tools. v7.13: listed definitions strip `aliases`; dispatch falls through to inactive modules (hidden aliases); readMcpToolsConfig reads mcp.tools.enable / legacy_listing.'
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - tool-loading
      - mcp
  compliance-checker:
    description: Shared compliance checking logic — purpose coverage, portal gates, aspect anchors, code quality
    type: service
    tags:
      - feature
      - review
      - compliance
  DocsLoader:
    description: Reads scan-index, .purpose files, portal.yaml, and flows.yaml to produce structured documentation page data
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - docs
  graduation-types:
    description: Type definitions for the automation tier graduation system — GraduationState, GraduationConfig, GraduationTier, NON_GRADUATABLE_CHECK_TYPES
    type: types
    tags:
      - feature
      - graduation
      - automation
  graduation-store:
    description: YAML read/write for .paradigm/graduation.yaml — state accessors, mutations, 30s cache
    type: store
    tags:
      - feature
      - graduation
      - persistence
  graduation-engine:
    description: Core graduation logic — eligibility checking against practice events, graduate/demote actions, failure tracking
    type: engine
    tags:
      - feature
      - graduation
      - automation
  aspect-fingerprint:
    description: Phase 3 content fingerprint search — Levenshtein distance, sliding window, structural hashing, cross-file search for relocated anchors
    type: engine
    tags:
      - feature
      - drift-detection
      - fingerprint
  event-stream:
    description: Ambient event stream — emit, store (JSONL), query, and attention-score events for ambient coordination. Append-only with automatic pruning.
    type: engine
    anchors:
      - event-stream.ts:1-199
    tags:
      - feature
      - ambient
      - event-stream
  data-policy-loader:
    description: Data policy loader — reads .paradigm/data-policy.yaml, merges with defaults, enforces trust rings, observation rules, content redaction, and per-agent overrides.
    type: loader
    anchors:
      - data-policy-loader.ts:1-195
    tags:
      - feature
      - data-policy
      - sovereignty
  work-log-loader:
    description: Work Log CRUD — record/search/summarize what agents did. Date-partitioned YAML in .paradigm/work-log/{date}/
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - knowledge-streams
      - work-log
  journal-loader:
    description: Learning Journal CRUD — record/search/stats for agent learnings. Agent-private YAML in ~/.paradigm/agents/{id}/journal/
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - knowledge-streams
      - journal
  decision-loader:
    description: 'Team Decisions CRUD — record/search/supersede institutional decisions. YAML in .paradigm/decisions/. v6.0 sub-phase 1: updateDecision accepts absorbed ADR fields (context/consequences/date/migrated_from/supersedes); supersedeDecision backfills supersedes[] on the new entry (D2 Loid addendum); exposes writeCompanionLoreEntry helper for D3 companion-lore writes (not yet wired — sub-phase 2 wires the tool handler).'
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - knowledge-streams
      - decisions
      - v6.0
  nomination-engine:
    description: 'Nomination engine — processes events into agent nominations and debates. Core loop: event → attention scoring → nomination → debate detection → surfacing. 7.12.0: `work-completed` events never nominate (NON_NOMINATING_EVENT_TYPES, D1 — they stay in stream.jsonl). Journal-to-notebook promotion (autoPromoteJournalEntries — pattern_discovered + human_feedback) is gated by the BELIEF-DELTA gate decidePromotion() with configurable bands loadPromotionBands() (config.yaml learning.promotion.{floor,deltaMin,epsilon,novelBar}; defaults 0.7/0.10/0.05/0.8, uncalibrated) — prior from notebookPrior (never journal confidence_before); absolute 0.8 survives only as the novel-concept fallback; human_feedback is floor-only; each candidate appends a promotion-decisions.jsonl row with gate:belief-delta-v1, reason, shadow absoluteWouldPromote, after:null when missing (kills the ?? 0 artifact); a small rise (epsilon <= delta < deltaMin) is reason below-delta, distinct from hold-silence (|delta| < epsilon); the shadow bar is LEGACY_ABSOLUTE_BAR; certifiedBy:gate, or certifiedBy:human for human_feedback promotions. The GATED single-entry path (gatedPromoteJournalEntry — /class sign-off, human ruling IS the gate, NEVER the delta gate, certifiedBy:peer|quorum, no instrument row; TD-2026-06-25-044), Neverland validation metrics, stale nomination expiry (7-day), reason storage on engage, Symphony relay forwarding, and surfacing config.'
    type: engine
    anchors:
      - nomination-engine.ts:1
    tags:
      - feature
      - ambient
      - nominations
      - debates
      - learning
      - surfacing
      - neverland
  session-work-log:
    description: 'Session work log — JSONL append log capturing agent contributions and user verdicts during a session. Read by Maestro at postflight for targeted learning feedback. Bounded at 200 entries, cleared on session start. Also hosts the durable iteration-revision channel (readPendingIterationRevisions / markIterationRevisionsConsumed, IterationRevisionEntry) — agent belief-revisions from iteration loops, kept separate from the human-verdict channel and routed to the self_reflection journal trigger. T-2026-06-13-004 adds the postflight-liveness channel (recordPostflightLiveness / readPostflightLiveness, PostflightLivenessRecord → .paradigm/events/postflight-liveness.jsonl) — every non-dry-run postflight pass appends one durable row (postflight-live when it journaled, postflight-noop{reason} when it did not) so a broken loop is no longer byte-identical to a healthy one (the falsifiable liveness invariant `paradigm doctor` reads).'
    type: loader
    anchors:
      - session-work-log.ts:1
    tags:
      - feature
      - maestro
      - learning
      - session
    components:
      - '#activity-metrics'
  agent-state:
    description: Per-project + global state tracking for agent continuity. Tracks last session summary, pending work, decisions, patterns, and career stats across sessions.
    type: service
    flows:
      - $agent-learning-loop
    signals:
      - '!agent-state-recorded'
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/agent-state.ts
  gap-narrator:
    description: Human-readable narration engine for enforcement check gaps. Produces explanations and fix instructions for 13 check types (missing-purpose, missing-gates, aspect-drift, stale-purpose, unregistered-symbol, unregistered-event, missing-flow, uncovered-endpoint, uncovered-gate, uncovered-flow, undocumented-aspect, missing-tests, missing-lore). Used by doctor --explain and postflight report generation.
    type: engine
    file: gap-narrator.ts
  activity-metrics:
    description: 'Proxy metrics tracking for session activity. Records tool call count, payload size, and session duration per agent. No dollar figures or token counts. Types: ActivityMetric, SessionActivitySummary. Functions: recordActivityMetric(), getSessionActivitySummary(), clearActivityMetrics().'
    type: service
    components:
      - '#session-work-log'
  soft-provenance:
    description: Optional parentId and lineageType fields on NotebookEntry for tracking derivation chains without DAG validation. Enables notebook promotion lineage tracking (promoted-from-lore, derived-from-notebook, manual-input). Used by paradigm_notebook_add tool and prepareForPublish() ringfencing.
    type: service
    components:
      - '#notebook-loader'
  outcome-reference-tracking:
    description: Records which notebook entries were loaded into agent prompts during orchestration. Pure data collection — no scoring or attribution.
    type: utility
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/session-work-log.ts
  compliance-health:
    description: Tracks stop hook violation frequency over time and computes compliance trends (improving/stable/degrading). Powers Conductor health dot.
    type: utility
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/compliance-health.ts
  provisional-intake:
    description: 'Provisional-candidate intake (T-2026-06-13-004) — the floor-trust session miner that lets the loop LEARN FROM FAILURE without breaching the classroom gate. mineProvisionalCandidates(rootDir, projectName, fallbackClaimant) reads already-recorded failure signals (overrides.jsonl, dismissed/revised durable verdicts) and stages each as a journal entry stamped provenance {source:external, trust:external} with the NON-promotable failure_analysis trigger, tagged provisional-candidate/floor-trust. Invoked once per session-boundary postflight pass; idempotent via .paradigm/events/provisional-mined.jsonl. Invisible to autoPromoteJournalEntries (which only promotes pattern_discovered/human_feedback) so nothing reaches a notebook or CLAUDE.md until the gated Classroom adjudicates it.'
    type: engine
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/provisional-intake.ts
    tags:
      - feature
      - learning
      - classroom
    components:
      - '#journal-loader'
      - '#session-work-log'
  orchestration-marker:
    description: 'v7 "Teeth" T-005 — single best-effort writer of the .paradigm/.orchestrated enforcement marker that satisfies the Stop-hook orchestration-required gate. recordOrchestrationCompletion(rootDir, {verdicts, source}) writes { timestamp, type:orchestrated, verdicts, source }. Called ONLY from real completion signals (a chainLive settlement in task-settlement.ts, or a debrief with real agent verdicts in captain.ts) — never on orchestrate_inline tool entry. Enforcement now verifies completion (verdicts>0), not invocation. Write failures are logged and swallowed so settlement/debrief never break. Source union is settlement | debrief | delegation: the delegation source is written by the Claude Code PostToolUse Agent|Task shell hook (#delegation-hook, claude-code-delegation.sh) with the same payload shape plus a subagent field. Readers honour the marker by age (PARADIGM_GATE_TTL_HOURS, default 4h).'
    type: utility
    tags:
      - enforcement
      - team-funnel
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/orchestration-marker.ts
  yaml-validator:
    description: Fail-closed YAML loader returning a discriminated union (missing/unparseable/invalid/ok). Classifies YAMLException by reason into duplicate-key/syntax/other; detail strings are redacted classifiers only — never file contents, gate names, or route paths. Optional zod schema validation. v5.37.12 security patch (2026-04-22 audit). v5.38.0 re-exports classifyYamlError from @a-company/portal-core (single source of truth) and honors PARADIGM_STRICT=1 by throwing on non-ok results.
    type: utility
    tags:
      - security
      - fail-closed
      - portal
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/yaml-validator.ts
  write-and-confirm:
    description: v5.38.0 atomic-write + read-back verify wrapper for mutation handlers. Writes to .tmp sibling then renames; re-reads the file; runs verify callback; throws WriteVerificationError on failure. Returns WriteEnvelope with truncated HMAC (first 12 hex chars of HMAC-SHA256 keyed with per-install secret) and byte count. Applied to portal_add_gate, portal_add_route, purpose_add_component, purpose_link, purpose_remove. Logs redacted — no gate names or file paths in error surfaces.
    type: utility
    tags:
      - security
      - fail-closed
      - mutation-safety
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/write-and-confirm.ts
  consistency-tracker:
    description: v5.38.0 round-trip consistency audit log. Records transformation CLASSES (prefix-stripped/array-coerced/default-applied/duplicate-key-detected/case-normalized) with fixed surface classifiers (portal.yaml/purpose.yaml) and counts — never gate names, route paths, or file contents. One injectable singleton per reindex pass; report rendered into paradigm_reindex envelope and .paradigm/manifest.consistency.json. Lossy transformations trigger strict-mode reindex failure.
    type: engine
    tags:
      - security
      - redacted
      - portal
      - consistency
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/consistency-tracker.ts
  strict-mode:
    description: v5.38.0 PARADIGM_STRICT=1 env var gate. Default OFF; flip ON in v5.39.0 after field observation. In strict mode, safeLoad throws on any non-ok/non-missing result, reindex fails on lossy transformations, and writeAndConfirm verify failures are never downgraded.
    type: utility
    tags:
      - security
      - fail-closed
      - configuration
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/strict-mode.ts
  wisdom-loader:
    description: 'Reads team wisdom from .paradigm/wisdom/ — preferences/antipatterns/expertise. 30s TTL cache, invalidated on writes. Global antipatterns/preferences merged from ~/.paradigm/wisdom/ (local wins on id collision). 7.12.0 (D2): the legacy wisdom/decisions read path is REMOVED (project and global) — WisdomContext.decisions is always []; canonical decisions live in .paradigm/decisions/ (#decision-loader); `paradigm migrate learning-stores` moves leftovers. recordDecision (legacy writer) is @deprecated.'
    type: loader
    tags:
      - feature
      - knowledge-streams
      - wisdom
      - v6.0
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/wisdom-loader.ts
  learning-stores:
    description: 'Learning-stores registry (7.12.0, D5) — READ-ONLY facade listLearningStores(rootDir) naming every learning store with class (ledger|knowledge|pipeline|policy|native), path, scope, owner and a never-throwing count(). Classes follow the spec''s three conceptual stores: ledger = lore (counts .lore/.yaml under lore/entries/<date>/), work-log, history, raw journals; knowledge = decisions, antipatterns, notebooks, protocols, skills, preferences; pipeline = event-stream, nominations, debates + the promotion-decisions / classroom-certifications / notebook-refs / liveness instruments. Encodes Loid''s must-NOT-consolidate list as separate rows (journals vs notebooks; the instruments; decisions vs antipatterns). Habits = policy (hook policy, D3). Claude Code native memory registered read-only, never migrated. Used by the doctor census and migrate learning-stores.'
    type: registry
    tags:
      - learning
      - v7.12
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/learning-stores.ts
  protocol-loader:
    description: 'Loads/validates .paradigm/protocols/*.protocol and rebuilds the protocol index. 7.12.0 (D4): lintProtocol emits PROTOCOL_IS_SKILL (warn only, never changes status; surfaced in validateProtocol issues) when no step names a repo path — the reverse of skill-loader''s SKILL_IS_PROTOCOL, reusing its exported repoPathTokens detector.'
    type: loader
    tags:
      - protocols
      - skills
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/protocol-loader.ts
  global-store:
    description: 'Cross-project wisdom store at ~/.paradigm/wisdom/ (antipatterns, preferences, decisions). 7.12.0 (D2): loadGlobalDecisions is @deprecated and no longer part of the wisdom read path — retained only for the promote-to-global duplicate check in tools/wisdom.ts.'
    type: store
    tags:
      - wisdom
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/global-store.ts
  arch-loader:
    description: Symbol architecture loader — reads and resolves project symbol graph for arch tools. Provides structured access to component hierarchy, flows, gates, and signals for the Atlas cartographer agent.
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/arch-loader.ts
    type: loader
  calibration-aggregate:
    description: 'Calibration aggregation (#calibration, T-011) — the MCP-side learned-table rebuild that both `paradigm calibrate` and the settlement chain call (aggregate-on-settle). aggregateActuals(lines) groups estimate-actuals by (archetype, taskType) into p10/p90 bands at n>=8; rebuildLearnedTable(rootDir) reads the actuals and writes token-estimates.json (best-effort, idempotent). Extracted from the CLI so the MCP settlement chain can close the calibration loop without importing the CLI package.'
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/calibration-aggregate.ts
    type: utility
    tags: [feature, calibration, learning-loop]
  skill-loader:
    description: 'Skills Phase 1 (T-2026-09-26-002) — the ONE loader/validator for agent-owned SKILL.md sources (project .paradigm/skills/<id> › global ~/.paradigm/skills/<id>; SkillEnv makes homedir/globalDir injectable). parseSkill/serializeSkill (round-trip), resolveSkill, listSkills(Detailed), lintSkill (SKILL_IS_PROTOCOL, SKILL_IS_NOTEBOOK, OWNED_SKILL_CAP, missing notebook/protocol, unresolved steward, kebab name, semver), computeContentHash (sha256 of canonical frontmatter minus certification + body + references/assets/scripts), checkPins (paradigm_* hashed against injected listToolDefinitions; host/* never checked; third-party unknown unless a tools/list dump is supplied), computeStatus (invalid › stale › ok › uncertified — never stored), resolveAgentSkills for enrichment, and the PURE $skill-certification verifier evaluateCertification (TTY, founder, lint, pins, ≥1 scenario with fixture + non-steward probe on skill:<id>@<ver> + human-confirmed survival) + applyCertification + buildSkillCertRow (kind skill ledger row). Imported by #skill-cli by relative path; certification is CLI-only (never an MCP tool). Fix pass: KEBAB id guard (isValidSkillId/assertSkillId) on every id that becomes a path; DIR_ID_MISMATCH + RESOURCE_SYMLINK lint errors; NOTEBOOK_MISSING warns for bundled; certification is drift-detection (not tamper-proof; signing = follow-up) — ok requires the SKILL.md block AND a matching kind skill ledger row (loadSkillCertLedger = project classroom ledger + global ~/.paradigm/events/skill-certifications.jsonl via appendGlobalSkillCertRow); evaluateCertification needs env, a resolvable non-steward probe agent and an existing fixture; listSkillScripts lists scripts/ with sha256 for certify; resolveAgentSkills uses cached structural lint only (no notebook scan, pins unchecked). v7.11 pack scope: third, lowest-precedence read-only scope `pack` (project › global › pack) from university-core discoverPacks skillDirs (SkillEnv.packSkillDirs injectable; only probed when <root>/.paradigm exists); parseSkill FORCES trust external + drops certification for scope pack; dir basename must equal meta.id; listPackSkills(env) → PackSkillEntry[] {packId, skill, scriptCount, shadowedBy?} (all pack skills incl. shadowed — backs Platform Academy /skills + pack_list); findPackSkill; importPackSkill(packId, id, {env, scope}) copies SKILL.md + resources (no symlinks/dotfiles) as trust provisional, provenance.source pack, upstream <pack>:<id>@<ver>, never overwrites; lint PACK_SHADOWED warn both directions; steward/protocol/notebook resolution downgraded to warn for pack scope; pack skills excluded from OWNED_SKILL_CAP. v7.11 fix pass: resolveSkill(id, env, {includePack}) — a project/global source that exists but fails to parse resolves to null (no fall-through to global/pack); resolveAgentSkills passes includePack:false so pack skills never reach agent prompts / Your Skills. importPackSkill takes expectedHash (refused content-changed on mismatch) and lstats each resource file right before copying (refused symlink). v7.12 (D8): splitFrontmatter is a thin strict wrapper over premise-core #frontmatter-parser — same exported signature ({data, body}) and the same error strings, pinned by skill-loader-frontmatter.test.ts.'
    type: loader
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/skill-loader.ts
    flows:
      - $skill-certification
    tags: [feature, skills, classroom]
  aspect-graph:
    description: 'SQLite aspect graph utils (.paradigm/aspect-graph.db): materializeAspects, ripple, heatmap, checkDrift. v7.12 (D9) section anchors: anchors table gains anchor_kind TEXT DEFAULT ''lines'' + anchor_key TEXT via idempotent ALTER migrations (PRAGMA table_info guard + catch; safe twice, safe on pre-7.12 DBs). Heading/block anchors resolve to the section''s CURRENT line range at materialize (premise-core resolveSectionAnchorLines; 0/0 when unresolvable) with baseline hashes; checkDrift re-resolves the KEY first then hashes the range — moved section = clean (row lines updated, .purpose untouched), whitespace = cosmetic, content change = modified, renamed/removed heading or block = missing (exists:true, drifted). No git line-shift or content-search heal for section anchors. Line anchors (anchor_kind lines) are byte-identical to before.'
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/aspect-graph.ts
    tags: [aspect-graph, drift, anchors]
  docs-loader:
    description: 'Docs section loader (config, portal, university index, markdown guides). v7.12 (D8): its private parseFrontmatter is a null-returning adapter over premise-core #frontmatter-parser (lenient) — no block or malformed YAML → null; non-mapping → frontmatter {}; now also accepts CRLF and a closing fence at EOF.'
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/docs-loader.ts
    tags: [docs, frontmatter]
  skill-projector:
    description: 'Skills Phase 1 — one-way projection of certified skill sources to ~/.claude/skills/pdg-<id>/ (or <root>/.claude/skills with target project). Gates: lint errors, stale pins, trust (only status ok; allowProvisional injects the PROVISIONAL banner). Rewrites name pdg-<id>, FLATTENS metadata.paradigm to a string map (paradigm-id/version/steward/trust/source), drops certification, writes .pdg-generated.json marker; refuses unmarked or downstream-drifted dests and HARD-REFUSES anything under ~/.claude/skills/synced/ (symlink-aware). Atomic temp-dir + rename; idempotent. adoptSkill pulls downstream edits back: patch+1, provisional, provenance adopted, certification dropped, prior archived to .versions/<ver>/, metadata un-flattened preserving source-only fields, re-projected under a fresh marker. Fix pass: scripts/ never projected for non-certified skills (marker.scriptsWithheld); any symlink in a projected dir = drift; dotfiles ignored in the drift hash; stale .pdg-*.tmp-* swept; synced/ checked first; adopt refuses source-changed (unless force) and widened allowed-tools (unless confirmAllowedTools), returns frontmatterDiff, validates semver before the .versions path, and lints before re-projecting (reprojected:false on errors). v7.11: projectSkill refuses scope pack (untrusted, hint `paradigm skill import <pack>:<id>`); adoptSkill never treats a pack source as writable (not-found).'
    type: service
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/skill-projector.ts
    tags: [feature, skills]
  skill-usage:
    description: 'Skills Phase 1 — append-only .paradigm/events/skill-usage.jsonl (pruned to 500, modelled on appendFieldFailure). Rows carry entryId skill:<id>@<ver>, the same key as the scenario probe and the cert row. buildSkillUsageRow maps a host Skill invocation pdg-<id> to the skill id + version from the projection sidecar (for the PostToolUse Skill hook). Fix pass: KEBAB-validates the id, trusts only a marker whose skillId matches; resolveHookProjectDir prefers CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR over payload cwd.'
    type: service
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/skill-usage.ts
    signals:
      - '!skill-used'
    tags: [feature, skills, learning-loop]
  persona-sentinel-validation:
    description: 'personas-loader validateAgainstSentinel — matches each persona journey step to its latest paradigm-personas Sentinel event (persona.step.complete / persona.step.fail, filtered by run_id, chain_id, environment). queryEvents returns newest first, so events are replayed oldest to newest and the latest event per step decides pass or fail. Reads GenericEvent.data (previously a non-existent data_json, so no step ever matched).'
    type: service
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/personas-loader.ts
    tags: [personas, sentinel]
  portal-routes:
    description: 'Single accessor for portal.yaml routes. portalRoutes(gateConfig) returns [] because portal-core parseGateConfig drops routes (T-2026-10-22-002, owned by Aegis); fix it here and paradigm_gates_for_route, pm preflight/postflight and habits evaluation all pick it up. parsePortalRoutes(raw) reads the raw YAML routes map (gate list or { gates, method }) and is used for workspace siblings.'
    type: utility
    file: packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/portal-routes.ts
    tags: [portal, security]
